Falsifies `file_allocation_table::long_name::verification::every_numbered_alias_carries_its_number`.

The defect: the digits of the number go into the tail in reverse, so the twelfth collision writes ~21 and the alias no longer says which number it is, and two names can share one.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(read, number)`.

diff --git a/crates/file_allocation_table/src/long_name.rs b/crates/file_allocation_table/src/long_name.rs
--- a/crates/file_allocation_table/src/long_name.rs
+++ b/crates/file_allocation_table/src/long_name.rs
@@ -142,7 +142,7 @@ impl LongName {
             rest /= 10;
         }
         rest = number;
-        for at in (1..=digits).rev() {
+        for at in 1..=digits {
             tail[at] = b'0' + (rest % 10) as u8;
             rest /= 10;
         }
